  "$comment": "Controlled vocabulary for reading imaging report text (AGENTS.md Sections 105, 107, 111, 113). Organs map anatomy words to body-model structure ids; paired organs take a side only from the words 'right'/'left' in the same sentence. Regions map words to region ids in regions.json ({side} is replaced by left/right). A position region (pole, lobe) is chosen over a tissue region (cortex, medulla, pelvis) when a sentence names one of each; two of the same kind means no region is chosen. Finding words only decide THAT a sentence states something about an organ; the report's own words are always quoted, never rewritten. Negation cues mean the finding is not present and is never marked. Words are matched case-insensitively on word boundaries. Bones (X-ray): each bone maps to its own body-model structure; adjectives shared with vessels, nerves or sinuses are not used. Chest X-ray zones name the lung and side only, never a lobe. Long-bone regions (proximal end, shaft, distal end) are overlay markers.",
